<h3><span>Major spoilers below, do not read if you've not already read SCP-3211</span></h3>
<p>If you've spoken to someone else who's read this then you'll have noticed that there are multiple versions of this document. You only get to read one, but someone else might have been given a different one to read. It is selected randomly, and represents the fact that your in-universe &quot;researcher&quot; has generated a false memory, as detailed in the document. The first version of the document that you read represents this false memory.</p>
<p>Of course, it's not fair to only let you read it once - what if you prefer to read slowly? - so here's a few tips for you.</p>
<hr />
<p>If you want to see the original version again, on the starting page click &quot;AUTHORISATION&quot; at the bottom, then click the button &quot;Ignore seen&quot; that appears, then click &quot;Proceed&quot;</p>
<p>(to get to the starting page, just refresh the page)</p>
<p>If you want to make the document completely forget you've read it, click &quot;Reset&quot;</p>
<p>If you want to manually select a new version of the SCP to read, click &quot;Reset&quot; then one of the numbers 0 - 3.</p>
<p>To stop the timer, click &quot;Stop timer&quot; while the timer is running</p>
<p>To get a running log of what the SCP is doing, open up the JavaScript console (Ctrl+Shift+I on Chrome)</p>
